'''X.AI Corp.''', [[Trade name|doing business as]] '''xAI''', is an American company working in the area of [[artificial intelligence]] (AI), [[social media]] and [[technology]].<ref name="OpenCorporates">{{Cite web |title=X.AI Corp. |url=https://opencorporates.com/companies/us_nv/E28915122023-8 |access-date=2023-07-27 |website=[[OpenCorporates]] |archive-date=August 5, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230805051958/https://opencorporates.com/companies/us_nv/E28915122023-8 |url-status=live }}</ref> Founded by [[Elon Musk]] in 2023, the company's flagship product is a [[generative AI]] chatbot named [[Grok (chatbot)|Grok]].

== History ==
xAI was founded on March 9, 2023, by Musk.<ref>{{cite web |date=July 12, 2023 |title=Elon Musk launches xAI in challenge to dominance of ChatGPT owner |url=https://www.ft.com/content/19cce4b5-b2dd-4c1e-a109-b500e504dbb6 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230712183908/https://www.ft.com/content/19cce4b5-b2dd-4c1e-a109-b500e504dbb6 |archive-date=July 12, 2023 |access-date=July 12, 2023 |newspaper=[[Financial Times]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Bhattacharya |first=Suryathapa |date=July 12, 2023 |title=Elon Musk Launches xAI, His New Artificial-Intelligence Company |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/elon-musk-xai-artificial-intelligence-company-openai-chatgpt-4a6f178a |url-access=subscription |url-status= |archive-url= |archive-date= |access-date=July 12, 2023 |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]]}}</ref> For Chief Engineer, he recruited Igor Babuschkin, formerly associated with [[Google DeepMind|Google's DeepMind unit]].<ref name="Isaacson2023">{{cite book |last1=Isaacson |first1=Walter |author-link=Walter Isaacson |url=https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Elon-Musk/Walter-Isaacson/9781982181284 |title=Elon Musk |date=September 12, 2023 |publisher=Simon & Schuster |isbn=978-1-9821-8128-4 |pages=605–606 |access-date=28 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231126180200/https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Elon-Musk/Walter-Isaacson/9781982181284 |archive-date=November 26, 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> Musk officially announced the formation of xAI on July 12, 2023.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Vynck |first=Gerrit De |date=2023-07-15 |title=Musk's new AI company, xAI, will aim to solve scientific mysteries |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2023/07/14/xai-elon-musk-ai-company/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230717133426/https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2023/07/14/xai-elon-musk-ai-company/ |archive-date=July 17, 2023 |access-date=2023-07-17 |newspaper=Washington Post |language=en-US |issn=0190-8286}}</ref>

As of July 2023, xAI was headquartered in the [[San Francisco Bay Area]].<ref>{{cite web |author=Anirban Ghoshal |date=July 13, 2023 |title=Elon Musk launches xAI to take on ChatGPT-maker OpenAI |url=https://www.computerworld.com/article/3702708/elon-musk-launches-xai-to-take-on-chatgpt-maker-openai.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230718163752/https://www.computerworld.com/article/3702708/elon-musk-launches-xai-to-take-on-chatgpt-maker-openai.html |archive-date=July 18, 2023 |access-date=July 14, 2023 |website=Computer World}}</ref> It was initially incorporated in [[Nevada]] as a [[benefit corporation|public-benefit corporation]] with the stated general purpose of "creat[ing] a material positive impact on society and the environment".<ref>{{cite web |last=Peterson |first=Becky |date=2023-12-26 |title=Musk's xAI Incorporates as Benefit Corporation With 'Positive Impact' Goal |url=https://www.theinformation.com/articles/musks-xai-incorporates-as-benefit-corporation-with-positive-impact-goal |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250801164528/https://www.theinformation.com/articles/musks-xai-incorporates-as-benefit-corporation-with-positive-impact-goal |archive-date=2025-08-01 |access-date=26 August 2025 |website=The Information |language=en}}</ref> By May 2024, it had dropped the public-benefit status, as revealed by media reports in August 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kolodny |first=Lora |date=2025-08-25 |title=Elon Musk's xAI secretly dropped its benefit corporation status while fighting OpenAI |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2025/08/25/elon-musk-xai-dropped-public-benefit-corp-status-while-fighting-openai.html |access-date=2025-08-26 |website=CNBC |language=en}}</ref>  The original stated [[Mission statement|goal of the company]] was "to understand the true nature of the universe".<ref name=":12">{{Cite web |title=xAI: Understand the Universe |url=http://x.ai/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230803163337/https://x.ai/ |archive-date=2023-08-03 |access-date=2023-08-03 |website=x.ai |language=en}}</ref>

=== Financial history ===
In November 2023, Musk stated that "X Corp investors will own 25% of xAI".<ref>{{Cite news |title=Elon Musk (@elonmusk) on X |url=https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1726177644671091192 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241003164205/https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1726177644671091192 |archive-date=October 3, 2024 |access-date=2025-07-24 |work=X (formerly Twitter) |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref> In December 2023, in a [[U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission|U.S. Securities Exchange Commission]] (SEC) filing, xAI revealed that it had raised US$134.7 million in outside funding out of a total of up to $1 billion.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Silberling |first1=Amanda |title=Elon Musk is looking to raise $1 billion for xAI |url=https://techcrunch.com/2023/12/05/elon-musk-raise-1-billion-xai/ |access-date=6 December 2023 |archive-date=December 6, 2023 | work=TechCrunch |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231206102200/https://techcrunch.com/2023/12/05/elon-musk-raise-1-billion-xai/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Primack |first=Dan |date=December 6, 2023 |title=How Elon Musk may be spinning up a Plan B to save X |url=https://www.axios.com/2023/12/06/elon-musk-twitter-x-ai-funding |access-date=2024-09-06 |website=axios.com |archive-date=November 13, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241113010459/https://www.axios.com/2023/12/06/elon-musk-twitter-x-ai-funding |url-status=live }}</ref> After the earlier raise, Musk stated in December 2023 that xAI was not seeking any funding "right now".<ref name="reuters20231206">{{Cite web |date=December 6, 2023 |title=Elon Musk says his AI firm xAI is not raising funds 'right now' |url=https://www.reuters.com/technology/elon-musk-says-his-ai-firm-xai-is-not-raising-funds-right-now-2023-12-06/ |access-date=2024-09-06 |website=reuters.com}}</ref> By May 2024, xAI was reportedly planning to raise another $6 billion of funding.<ref>{{cite news |last=Tomchak |first=David |date=30 May 2024 |title=Elon Musk: Tesla CEO warns of the risks of AI to our jobs—while raising $6bn for xAI |work=Standard.co.uk |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/news/tech/elon-musk-tesla-ai-risks-jobs-xai-b1160911.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240530121236/https://www.standard.co.uk/news/tech/elon-musk-tesla-ai-risks-jobs-xai-b1160911.html |archive-date=30 May 2024 |access-date=30 May 2024}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=May 18, 2024 |title=Elon's AI venture being sold as part of a "Muskonomy" |url=https://www.axios.com/2024/05/18/elon-musk-xai-fundraising |work=Axios |archive-date=November 13, 2024 |access-date=May 24, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241113010528/https://www.axios.com/2024/05/18/elon-musk-xai-fundraising |url-status=live }}</ref> Later that same month, the company secured the support of various [[venture capital]] firms, including [[Andreessen Horowitz]], [[Lightspeed Venture Partners]], [[Sequoia Capital]] and [[Tribe Capital]].<ref>{{Cite news |title=Elon Musk's xAI secures new backing from Andreessen, Lightspeed, Sequoia and Tribe |url=https://www.ft.com/content/0b6f634e-dbf0-4238-a319-1dc1bbc0b62e |access-date=2024-05-24 |website=Financial Times |date=May 23, 2024 |last1=Hammond |first1=George |last2=Kinder |first2=Tabby |archive-date=September 1, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240901124237/https://www.ft.com/content/0b6f634e-dbf0-4238-a319-1dc1bbc0b62e |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=May 23, 2024 |title=Musk's xAI seeking to raise $6 bln in Andreessen Horowitz-backed funding, FT reports |url=https://www.reuters.com/technology/musks-xai-seeking-raise-6-bln-andreessen-horowitz-backed-funding-ft-reports-2024-05-23/ |work=Reuters}}</ref>

{{as of|2024|8|df=US}}, Musk was diverting a large number of [[Nvidia]] chips that had been ordered by [[Tesla, Inc.]] to X and xAI.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kolodny |first1=Lora |title=Elon Musk ordered Nvidia to ship thousands of AI chips reserved for Tesla to X and xAI |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2024/06/04/elon-musk-told-nvidia-to-ship-ai-chips-reserved-for-tesla-to-x-xai.html |website=cnbc.com |date=June 4, 2024 |publisher=CNBC |access-date=10 August 2024 |archive-date=November 19, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241119203914/https://www.cnbc.com/2024/06/04/elon-musk-told-nvidia-to-ship-ai-chips-reserved-for-tesla-to-x-xai.html |url-status=live }}</ref> On December 23, 2024, xAI raised an additional $6 billion in a [[private capital|private]] funding round supported by [[Fidelity Investments|Fidelity]], [[BlackRock]], [[Sequoia Capital]], among others, making its total funding to date over $12 billion.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Conger |first=Kate |date=December 24, 2024 |title=Elon Musk's xAI Raises $6 Billion in New Funding |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/12/24/technology/elon-musk-xai-funding.html |work=[[The New York Times]] |archive-date=December 29, 2024 |access-date=December 29, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241229134155/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/12/24/technology/elon-musk-xai-funding.html |url-status=live }}</ref> On February 10, 2025, xAI and other investors made an offer to acquire [[OpenAI]] for $97.4 billion.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Hammond |first=George |date=2025-02-10 |title=Elon Musk-led consortium offers $100bn to take control of OpenAI |url=https://www.ft.com/content/3a673ed2-26d5-47af-9028-8af7d742c2e7 |access-date=2025-02-10 |work=Financial Times}}</ref> On March 17, 2025, xAI acquired Hotshot, a [[Startup company|startup]] working on [[Text-to-video model|AI-powered video generation tools]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wiggers |first=Kyle |date=2025-03-17 |title=Elon Musk's AI company, xAI, acquires a generative AI video startup |url=https://techcrunch.com/2025/03/17/elon-musks-ai-company-xai-acquires-a-generative-ai-video-startup/ |access-date=2025-03-17 |website=TechCrunch |language=en-US}}</ref> On March 28, 2025, Musk announced that xAI acquired sister company [[X Corp.]], the developer of the [[X (formerly Twitter)]] social media platform, which was previously acquired by Musk in October 2022. The deal, an all-stock transaction, valued X at $33 billion, with a full valuation of $45 billion when factoring in $12 billion in debt. Meanwhile, xAI itself was valued at $80 billion. Both companies were combined into a single entity called X.AI Holdings Corp.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Zeff |first=Maxwell |date=2025-03-29 |title=Elon Musk says xAI acquired X |url=https://techcrunch.com/2025/03/29/elon-musk-says-xai-acquired-x/ |access-date=2025-03-31 |website=TechCrunch |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-03-28 |title=Musk's xAI Startup Swallows Up X Social Network in Surprise Deal |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-03-28/musk-says-that-his-xai-startup-has-acquired-x-for-33-billion |website=Bloomberg |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hyatt |first=John |title=Elon Musk Scores $33 Billion In Self-Serving Merger |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/johnhyatt/2025/04/02/the-xai-x-deal-is-a-33-billion-windfall-for-elon-musk/ |access-date=2025-04-23 |website=Forbes |language=en}}</ref>

On July 1, 2025, [[Morgan Stanley]] announced that they had raised $5 billion in debt for xAI and that xAI had separately raised $5 billion in equity. The debt consists of secured notes and term loans. Morgan Stanley took no stake in the debt.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Tracy |first1=Matt |last2=Wang |first2=Echo |last3=Bautzer |first3=Tatiana |last4=Wang |first4=Echo |last5=Bautzer |first5=Tatiana |date=2025-06-10 |title=Morgan Stanley markets $5 billion for Elon Musk-owned xAI in loans, bonds, sources say |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/morgan-stanley-markets-5-billion-elon-musk-owned-xai-loans-bonds-sources-say-2025-06-10/ |access-date=2025-07-13 |work=Reuters |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-07-01 |title=Musk's xAI raises $5 billion each in fresh debt and equity, Morgan Stanley says |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/musks-xai-raises-5-billion-each-fresh-debt-equity-morgan-stanley-says-2025-07-01/ |access-date=2025-07-12 |work=Reuters |language=en}}</ref> [[SpaceX]], another Musk venture, was involved in the equity raise, agreeing to invest $2 billion in xAI.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jin |first1=Berber |last2=Peterson |first2=Becky |title=SpaceX to Invest $2 Billion Into Elon Musk's xAI |url=https://www.wsj.com/tech/spacex-to-invest-2-billion-into-elon-musks-xai-413934de |work=Wall Street Journal |access-date=13 July 2025 |url-access=subscription}}</ref> On July 14,  xAI announced "Grok for Government" and the [[United States Department of Defense]] announced that xAI had received a $200 million contract for AI in the military, along with [[Anthropic]], [[Google]], and OpenAI.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Brodkin |first=Jon |date=2025-07-15 |title=Grok's "MechaHitler" meltdown didn't stop xAI from winning $200M military deal |url=https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2025/07/groks-mechahitler-meltdown-didnt-stop-xai-from-winning-200m-military-deal/ |access-date=2025-07-16 |website=Ars Technica |language=en}}</ref> On September 12, xAI laid off 500 data annotation workers. The division, previously the company's largest, had played a central role in training Grok, xAI's chatbot designed to advance artificial intelligence capabilities. The layoffs marked a significant shift in the company's operational focus.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kay |first1=Grace |title=Elon Musk's xAI lays off hundreds of workers tasked with training Grok |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-xai-layoffs-data-annotators-2025-9 |access-date=16 September 2025 |work=Business Insider |publisher=Axel Springer SE |date=2025-09-12}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=xAI Layoffs Shock Tech Industry: 500 Data Annotation Workers Cut as AI Focus Shifts |url=https://beamstart.com/news/xai-reportedly-lays-off-500-17577795076322 |access-date=2025-09-15 |website=xAI Layoffs Shock Tech Industry: 500 Data Annotation Workers Cut as AI Focus Shifts {{!}} BEAMSTART |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-09-13 |title=xAI reportedly laid off at least 500 AI tutors working on Grok |url=https://www.engadget.com/ai/xai-reportedly-laid-off-at-least-500-ai-tutors-working-on-grok-130059624.html |access-date=2025-09-15 |website=Engadget |language=en-US}}</ref>

=== Environmental impact ===
In June 2024, the [[Greater Memphis Chamber]] announced xAI was planning on building [[Colossus (supercomputer)|Colossus]], the world's largest supercomputer, in [[Memphis, Tennessee]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Musk to Locate xAI Supercomputer in Memphis |url=https://www.memphisflyer.com/musk-locates-xai-in-memphis |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240929080046/https://www.memphisflyer.com/musk-locates-xai-in-memphis |archive-date=September 29, 2024 |access-date=2024-06-06 |website=MemphisFlyer}}</ref> After a 122-day construction, the supercomputer went fully operational in December 2024. Local government in Memphis has voiced concerns regarding the increased usage of electricity, 150 [[Watt#Megawattv|megawatts]] of power at peak, and while the agreement with the city is being worked out, the company has deployed 14 VoltaGrid portable [[gas-fired power plant|methane-gas powered generators]] to temporarily enhance the power supply.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Edwards |first=Benj |date=2024-07-24 |title=Elon Musk claims he is training "the world's most powerful AI by every metric" |url=https://arstechnica.com/information-technology/2024/07/elon-musk-claims-he-is-training-the-worlds-most-powerful-ai-by-every-metric/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240725065546/https://arstechnica.com/information-technology/2024/07/elon-musk-claims-he-is-training-the-worlds-most-powerful-ai-by-every-metric/ |archive-date=July 25, 2024 |access-date=2024-07-25 |website=Ars Technica |language=en-us}}</ref>

Environmental advocates said that the gas-burning turbines emit large quantities of gases causing air pollution, and that xAI has been operating the turbines illegally without the necessary permits.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2024-08-28 |title=Musk's xAI operating gas turbines without permits at data center, environmental group says |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/environment/musks-xai-operating-gas-turbines-without-permits-data-center-environmental-group-2024-08-28/ |work=Reuters}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Environmentalists urge health department to take action on xAI |url=https://dailymemphian.com/subscriber/article/45989/environmental-groups-urge-shelby-county-health-dept-action-xai-turbines-memphis |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241001222514/https://dailymemphian.com/subscriber/article/45989/environmental-groups-urge-shelby-county-health-dept-action-xai-turbines-memphis |archive-date=October 1, 2024 |access-date=2024-09-10 |website=Memphis Local, Sports, Business & Food News {{!}} Daily Memphian |language=en}}</ref> ''[[The New Yorker]]'' reported on May 6, 2025, that thermal-imaging equipment used by volunteers flying over the site showed at least 33 generators giving off heat, indicating that they were all running. The truck-mounted generators emit about the same amount of pollutants as the Tennessee Valley Authority's large gas-fired power plant nearby.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=McKibben |first=Bill |url=https://www.newyorker.com/news/the-lede/how-is-elon-musk-powering-his-supercomputer |title=How Is Elon Musk Powering His Supercomputer? |magazine=[[The New Yorker]] |date=May 6, 2025 |access-date=May 8, 2025}}</ref> The Shelby County Health Department granted xAI an air permit for the project in July 2025.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Taft |first=Molly |title=Despite Protests, Elon Musk Secures Air Permit for xAI |url=https://www.wired.com/story/xai-data-center-air-pollution-permit/ |access-date=2025-07-03 |magazine=[[Wired (magazine)|Wired]] |language=en-US |issn=1059-1028}}</ref>

== Products ==
According to Musk in July 2023, a [[political correctness|politically correct]] AI would be dangerously misleading, citing as an example the fictional [[HAL 9000]] from the 1968 film ''[[2001: A Space Odyssey]]''. Musk instead said that xAI would be "maximally truth-seeking". Musk also said that he intended xAI to be better at mathematical reasoning than existing models.<ref>{{cite news |last=Schreckinger |first=Ben |date=July 17, 2023 |title=Elon Musk's liberal-trolling AI plan has a core audience |work=[[Politico]] |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/17/ai-musk-chatgpt-xai-00106672 |access-date=July 19, 2023 |archive-date=October 11, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231011211915/https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/17/ai-musk-chatgpt-xai-00106672 |url-status=live }}</ref> On November 4, 2023, xAI unveiled [[Grok (chatbot)|Grok]], an AI [[chatbot]] that is integrated with [[X (social network)|X]]. xAI stated that when the bot is out of [[Beta release|beta]], it will only be available to X's [[Twitter#Premium|Premium+]] subscribers.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Neowin |first=Paul Hill |date=2023-11-04 |title=Elon Musk gives a glimpse at xAI's Grok chatbot |url=https://www.neowin.net/news/elon-musk-gives-a-glimpse-at-xais-grok-chatbot/ |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Neowin |language=en |archive-date=November 4, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104083748/https://www.neowin.net/news/elon-musk-gives-a-glimpse-at-xais-grok-chatbot/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/elon-musk-says-his-new-ai-bot-grok-will-have-sarcasm-and-access-to-x-information-b4e169de |title=Elon Musk Says His New AI Bot 'Grok' Will Have Sarcasm and Access to X Information |date=November 4, 2023 |publisher=Wall Street Journal |access-date=4 November 2023 |archive-date=4 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104171521/https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/elon-musk-says-his-new-ai-bot-grok-will-have-sarcasm-and-access-to-x-information-b4e169de |url-status=live }}</ref>

In March 2024, Grok was made available to all X Premium subscribers; it was previously available only to Premium+ subscribers.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Elon Musk Makes Grok AI Available to All Paying X Subscribers: What to Know |url=https://www.cnet.com/tech/elon-musk-makes-grok-ai-available-to-all-paying-x-subscribers-what-to-know/ |access-date=2024-08-20 |website=CNET |language=en |archive-date=August 20, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240820202838/https://www.cnet.com/tech/elon-musk-makes-grok-ai-available-to-all-paying-x-subscribers-what-to-know/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mehta |first=Ivan |date=2024-04-06 |title=X makes Grok chatbot available to premium subscribers |url=https://techcrunch.com/2024/04/05/x-makes-grok-chatbot-available-to-premium-subscribers/ |access-date=2024-08-20 |website=TechCrunch |language=en-US |archive-date=August 20, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240820202836/https://techcrunch.com/2024/04/05/x-makes-grok-chatbot-available-to-premium-subscribers/ |url-status=live}}</ref> On March 17, 2024, xAI released Grok-1 as [[open source]].<ref>{{Cite news |title=Elon Musk's Grok-1 goes open-source: What it means for users |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/elon-musks-grok-1-goes-open-source-what-is-means-for-users/articleshow/108589278.cms |access-date=2024-08-20 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257 |archive-date=August 20, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240820194138/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/elon-musks-grok-1-goes-open-source-what-is-means-for-users/amp_articleshow/108589278.cms |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=David |first=Emilia |date=2024-03-18 |title=xAI open sources Grok |url=https://www.theverge.com/2024/3/17/24097810/xai-open-source-grok-musk-generative-ai-llm |access-date=2024-08-20 |website=The Verge |language=en |archive-date=May 23, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240523164210/https://www.theverge.com/2024/3/17/24097810/xai-open-source-grok-musk-generative-ai-llm |url-status=live }}</ref> On March 29, 2024, Grok-1.5 was announced, with "improved reasoning capabilities" and a context length of 128,000 tokens.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Announcing Grok-1.5 |url=https://x.ai/blog/grok-1.5 |access-date=2024-08-20 |website=x.ai |language=en |archive-date=November 12, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241112010307/https://x.ai/blog/grok-1.5 |url-status=live }}</ref> On April 12, 2024, Grok-1.5 Vision (Grok-1.5V) was announced.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Grok-1.5 Vision Preview |url=https://x.ai/blog/grok-1.5v |access-date=2024-08-20 |website=x.ai |language=en |archive-date=November 19, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241119215228/https://x.ai/blog/grok-1.5v |url-status=live }}</ref>{{primary inline|date=April 2025}} On August 14, 2024, Grok-2 was made available to X Premium subscribers.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mehta |first=Ivan |date=2024-08-14 |title=xAI releases Grok-2, adds image generation on X |url=https://techcrunch.com/2024/08/13/xais-grok-can-now-generate-images-on-x/ |access-date=2024-08-20 |website=TechCrunch |language=en-US |archive-date=September 17, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240917222845/https://techcrunch.com/2024/08/13/xais-grok-can-now-generate-images-on-x/ |url-status=live }}</ref> It is the first Grok model with image generation capabilities.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Weatherbed |first=Jess |date=2024-08-14 |title=xAI's new Grok-2 chatbots bring AI image generation to X |url=https://www.theverge.com/2024/8/14/24220127/grok-ai-chatbot-beta-image-generation-x-xai-update |access-date=2024-08-20 |website=The Verge |language=en |archive-date=November 17, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241117000048/https://www.theverge.com/2024/8/14/24220127/grok-ai-chatbot-beta-image-generation-x-xai-update |url-status=live }}</ref>

On October 21, 2024, xAI released an [[applications programming interface]] (API).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wiggers |first=Kyle |date=2024-10-21 |title=xAI, Elon Musk's AI startup, launches an API |url=https://techcrunch.com/2024/10/21/xai-elon-musks-ai-startup-launches-an-api/ |access-date=2024-11-03 |website=TechCrunch |language=en-US |archive-date=November 24, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241124212240/https://techcrunch.com/2024/10/21/xai-elon-musks-ai-startup-launches-an-api/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On December 9, 2024, xAI released a [[text-to-image model]] named [[Aurora (text-to-image model)|Aurora]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wiggers |first=Kyle |date=2024-12-07 |title=Elon Musk's X gains a new image generator, Aurora |url=https://techcrunch.com/2024/12/07/elon-musks-x-gains-a-new-image-generator-aurora/ |access-date=2024-12-07 |website=TechCrunch |language=en-US |archive-date=December 7, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241207174002/https://techcrunch.com/2024/12/07/elon-musks-x-gains-a-new-image-generator-aurora/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On February 17, 2025, xAI released Grok-3, which includes a [[Reflection (artificial intelligence)|reflection]] feature. xAI also introduced a websearch function called DeepSearch.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wiggers |first=Kyle |date=2025-02-17 |title=Elon Musk's xAI releases its latest flagship model, Grok 3 |url=https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/17/elon-musks-ai-company-xai-releases-its-latest-flagship-ai-grok-3/ |access-date=2025-03-12 |website=TechCrunch |language=en-US}}</ref> In March 2025, xAI added an image editing feature to Grok, enabling users to upload a photo, describe the desired changes, and receive a modified version.<ref>{{Cite web |author1=Eric Hal Schwartz |date=2025-03-25 |title=I tried Grok's new AI image editing features – they're fun but won't replace Photoshop any time soon |url=https://www.techradar.com/computing/artificial-intelligence/i-tried-groks-new-ai-image-editing-features-theyre-fun-but-wont-replace-photoshop-any-time-soon |access-date=2025-03-25 |website=TechRadar |language=en}}</ref> Alongside this, xAI released DeeperSearch, an enhanced version of DeepSearch.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bastian |first=Matthias |date=2025-03-22 |title=Grok 3 adds deeper search and AI image editing capabilities |url=https://the-decoder.com/grok-3-adds-deeper-search-and-ai-image-editing-capabilities/ |access-date=2025-03-25 |website=THE DECODER |language=en-US}}</ref> On July 9, 2025, xAI unveiled Grok-4. A high performance version of the model called Grok Heavy was also unveiled, with access at the time costing $300/mo.<ref>{{cite web | title=Musk Admits Grok AI 'Lacks Common Sense,' Reveals Pricey $300 Monthly Plan | date=July 10, 2025 | url=https://www.pcmag.com/news/musk-admits-grok-ai-lacks-common-sense-reveals-pricey-300-monthly-plan }}</ref>

